  "details": "I developed a prefab that uses finalIK raycasts, but switched to VRC Raycasts for convenience's sake\n\nPeople started reporting that the prefab was triggering when it shouldn't, so I looked into it\n\nMy raycasts are set up to snap to end and disable the object when the raycast doesn't connect, and in-editor it does, but in-game it doesn't.\n\nThe two contacts floating out is where the prefab is always supposed to reset to, but as you can see in the second image, if I walk through one of the raycasts it gets stuck. Also they are not disabled\n\nThe objects being controlled by the raycast aren't parented to the raycast if that's relevant",
